# AB (Bernal)-stacked bilayer graphene, 4 C atoms/cell, vacuum along z --
# purpose-built for this example's multi-site BSSE demo case only (see
# README section 2.5). Real, well-known physics, not a toy: Bernal stacking
# shifts the top layer by the A->B sublattice vector, so 2 of the 4 atoms
# end up sitting directly above/below an atom in the other layer ("eclipsed"
# / dimer sites) while the other 2 sit above/below a hollow hexagon center
# ("non-eclipsed" sites) -- two genuinely different local coordination
# environments for the SAME element, carbon, related within each pair by
# the cell's own inversion symmetry (multiplicity 2 each). This is exactly
# the situation --bsse-multi-site exists for: a single flat BSSE reference
# for "carbon" would silently average over 2 physically different
# environments, so stb-cohesive builds one ghost cluster per site instead.
#
# a = 2.46 Ang (graphene's real in-plane lattice constant), interlayer
# spacing 3.35 Ang (real graphite/bilayer-graphene value), c = 20 Ang vacuum.

NumberOfSpecies    1
NumberofAtoms      4

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   6   C
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
  2.460000000   0.000000000   0.000000000
 -1.230000000   2.130423000   0.000000000
  0.000000000   0.000000000  20.000000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.000000000   0.000000000   0.416250000   1
  0.333333333   0.666666667   0.416250000   1
  0.333333333   0.666666667   0.583750000   1
  0.666666667   0.333333333   0.583750000   1
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
